course: dictionary
lesson: 896
title: One word, two meanings: bishop
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These words are its context, and they leave clues. «The Church of England is led by bishops, with the Archbishop of Canterbury as senior bishop.» The clues are church, led and senior, so a bishop here is a senior church leader.
explain: Now look at this: «Chess travelled to Persia, the Arab world and Europe and changed into the game we play today; the chaturanga elephant, standing next to the horse, became today's bishop.» The clue is the game. Here a bishop is a piece on a chess board.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. "The church is led by senior church leaders" makes sense. "The chess game is led by a senior church leader" does not. So the clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: A bishop is a senior leader in many Christian churches who looks after the priests and churches in a large area called a diocese.
fact: In chess, a bishop is a piece that moves any number of squares diagonally.
fact: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.»
fact: Each chess player starts the game with two bishops, one on light squares and one on dark.
fact: Some church bishops wear a tall pointed hat called a mitre and carry a crook-shaped staff.
exercise: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.» In this sentence, what is a bishop? | A large area of land | *A senior church leader | A chess piece that moves diagonally | A type of hat worn by children
exercise: In chess, how does a bishop move? | In an L shape | *Diagonally, any number of squares | Only one square at a time in any direction | Straight forward like a rook
exercise: «Chess travelled to Persia, the Arab world and Europe.» Find and copy one place name from this sentence. | chess | *Persia | game | today
test: «The Church of England is led by bishops, with the Archbishop of Canterbury as senior bishop.» What does bishop mean here? | A chess piece | *A senior church leader | A type of food | A kind of boat
test: "Move your bishop" is a chess instruction. What does it mean? | A tall tree in the garden | *Move the chess piece diagonally | Cook a cake for the bishop | A priest who leads a church
exam: «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA; episcopal means led by bishops.» What does episcopal mean? | Written in old books | Led by kings | *Led by bishops | A kind of chess game
